---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../../components/SectionHeader.astro';

const lastUpdated = '6 August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Essential 8 Knowledge Base Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the Essential 8 Knowledge Base app on iOS and Android."
  robots="noindex, follow"
>
  <section class="section legal">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="// app.privacy"
        title="Essential 8 Knowledge Base Privacy Policy"
        text={`Last updated: ${lastUpdated} AEST`}
      />

      <div class="notice surface-card">
        <p>
          This privacy policy applies to the Essential 8 Knowledge Base app on both iOS and Android. It is
          separate from the general MadDogWarner.com website privacy notice.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="content">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>
          Essential 8 Knowledge Base is an offline reference app for Australian system administrators
          working with the ASD Essential Eight in Windows environments.
        </p>
        <p>
          Essential 8 Knowledge Base has no accounts, no analytics, and makes no network requests of its
          own — nothing you enter is ever sent to the developer or any third party. Your assessment
          progress, notes and audit history are stored only on your device.
        </p>

        <h2>Data collection</h2>
        <p>
          Essential 8 Knowledge Base does not collect user data or device data, and nothing you enter
          reaches MadDogWarner or any third party. The app does not use:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>accounts or login</li>
          <li>analytics SDKs</li>
          <li>advertising SDKs</li>
          <li>tracking technologies</li>
          <li>in-app purchases</li>
          <li>remote databases or cloud sync</li>
          <li>crash reporting or telemetry services</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Device permissions</h2>
        <p>
          The app does not request access to the microphone, camera, location services, contacts, photos,
          or other device sensors. It also does not request health data, Bluetooth, calendars, or reminders.
        </p>

        <h2>Network access</h2>
        <p>
          The app makes no network requests of its own. The reference content is bundled with the app and
          is available offline.
        </p>
        <p>
          The app may include external reference links to resources such as ASD, ACSC, Microsoft, GitHub,
          or MadDogWarner. External reference links open in your browser, outside the app, and the
          destination website's own privacy practices apply.
        </p>

        <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
        <p>
          The app stores what you enter so it is still there next time you open it. That includes your
          assessment progress, notes, saved profiles, your Microsoft 365 Additional Controls mode, and — if
          you use Deep Audit Mode — a timestamped audit history entry for every status change you make.
        </p>
        <p>
          This data is stored only on your device. It is never transmitted to MadDogWarner or any third
          party. It leaves your device only if you export a backup yourself, or through your device's own
          system backup.
        </p>
        <p>
          On iOS, the app's data is included in your device's system backup, such as iCloud backup. That
          backup is governed by Apple's privacy terms, not by this policy, and you can exclude the app from
          it in your device settings. On Android, the app is excluded from Android's automatic backup, so
          its data is not copied to Google and does not leave your device unless you export it yourself.
        </p>

        <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
        <p>
          Because the app holds this data locally and never sends it anywhere, there is nothing held by
          MadDogWarner to retain, delete, export, or transfer. You can clear your progress and audit
          history inside the app, and removing the app from your device removes its locally stored data.
          Copies held in your own device backups are removed according to your device's backup settings.
        </p>

        <h2>Third parties</h2>
        <p>
          Essential 8 Knowledge Base does not share user data with third parties. External websites opened
          from reference links are outside the app and are governed by their own privacy notices.
        </p>

        <h2>Affiliation</h2>
        <p>
          Essential 8 Knowledge Base is not affiliated with or endorsed by ASD, ACSC, Microsoft, Apple,
          Google, or any other referenced organisation.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Privacy questions about Essential 8 Knowledge Base can be sent through the MadDogWarner contact
          page at <a href="/contact/">maddogwarner.com/contact/</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          This policy may be updated if the app's functionality or data handling changes. The updated date
          at the top of this page will be changed when this policy is revised.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-top: 5rem;
  }

  .notice {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  .notice p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .content {
    max-width: 78ch;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 2rem 0 0.7rem;
    color: #fff;
    font-family: "Space Grotesk", sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }

  p,
  li {
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0, 180, 255, 0.45);
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
</style>
